# Azure Zero to Hero

## What This Series Covers

This is a 25-day series designed to take complete beginners to job-ready and certification-ready on Microsoft Azure. The series covers Azure concepts theoretically and practically — with demos, projects, and interview Q&A sessions built in throughout.

**Series outcomes:**
- Job-ready for **Azure DevOps** positions (combined with DevOps fundamentals).
- Prepared to clear **AZ-900** (Azure Fundamentals) certification.
- Prepared to clear **AZ-104** (Azure Administrator) certification.

---

### Day 1 — Cloud Computing Fundamentals
Foundation concepts applicable to any cloud provider (AWS, Azure, GCP):
- Virtualization and Virtual Machines
- APIs
- Regions, Geographies, and Availability Zones
- Scalability, Elasticity, Agility
- High Availability and Disaster Recovery
- Load Balancing

> This day exists to ensure every term used in the series is familiar before Azure-specific content begins.

---

### Day 2 — Getting Started with Azure
- Creating an Azure account
- Regions and Availability Zones — Azure perspective
- IaaS, PaaS, and SaaS models — definitions and differences
- Which model is used in this series and why

---

### Day 3 — Resources, Resource Groups & Azure Resource Manager
- What is a resource in Azure
- What is a Resource Group and why it matters
- Azure Resource Manager (ARM) — the engine behind resource creation
- How all resources in Azure are managed through ARM

---

### Day 4 — Azure Virtual Machines & VM Scale Sets
- Creating a Virtual Machine on Azure
- Connecting to a Virtual Machine
- Deploying a first application on an Azure VM
- Virtual Machine Scale Sets — Azure's auto-scaling mechanism (equivalent to AWS Auto Scaling Groups)

---

### Day 5 — Azure Networking Services (Basics)
Core networking concepts explained with a real-world traffic flow example:
- Virtual Network (VNet) — equivalent to AWS VPC
- Subnets
- CIDR block ranges
- Routes and Route Tables
- Network Security Groups (NSG)
- Application Security Groups (ASG)
- **Demo included**

---

### Day 6 — Azure Networking Services (Advanced)
- Virtual Network Peering — connecting two VNets (equivalent to AWS VPC Peering)
- VNet Gateway — alternative method to connect VNets
- VPN Gateway — secure connectivity, important for security interviews
- Azure Load Balancer vs Azure Application Gateway — differences and when to use each
- CDN (Content Delivery Network) — advantages and use cases

---

### Day 7 — Interview Q&A: Cloud Computing, Azure Basics & Networking
Dedicated interview questions and answers covering:
- Cloud computing fundamentals (Day 1)
- Azure basics (Days 2–3)
- Compute — Virtual Machines and Scale Sets (Day 4)
- Networking concepts (Days 5–6)

> Self-evaluation checkpoint — test knowledge before moving to advanced topics.

---

### Day 8 — Project: Two-Tier Application Deployment on Azure
First project of the series:
- Deploy a complete two-tier application (frontend + backend) on Azure
- Uses networking and VM concepts covered in Days 1–7
- Proof of concept of a real-world deployment pattern

---

### Day 9 — Azure Storage Services
- Different types of Azure storage services
- Use cases for each storage type
- Practical demonstrations

---

### Day 10 — Azure CLI (Command Line Interface)
First introduction to scripting and automation on Azure:
- What Azure CLI is and why it matters for DevOps engineers
- Creating resources via shell scripting and Python scripting
- Automating resource creation (instead of using the Azure portal)
- CLI documentation walkthrough with multiple examples

---

### Day 11 — Azure Resource Manager (ARM) Templates
- Creating resources using ARM templates (declarative Infrastructure as Code)
- Different resource creation approaches covered so far:
- Portal (Days 1–9)
- CLI scripting (Day 10)
- ARM Templates (Day 11)
- Terraform (Day 24)

---

### Day 12 — Authentication & Identity Management
- Azure Active Directory concepts
- Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)
- Authentication and identity management on Azure
- Why this is placed at Day 12 (not Day 1 — unlike AWS): familiarity with Azure platform first makes these concepts easier to understand

---

### Day 13 — Monitoring Azure Resources
- Monitoring resource activity and health on Azure
- Tracking who created resources and when
- Azure Monitor — dashboards, alerts, and metrics
- Note: this is infrastructure monitoring, not application monitoring

---

### Day 14 — Introduction to Azure DevOps
Overview of the Azure DevOps platform:
- Azure Repos — Git-based source control
- Azure Boards — project and work item tracking
- Azure Pipelines — CI/CD
- All Azure DevOps services and their roles

---

### Day 15 — Project: CI (Continuous Integration) with Azure DevOps
- Hands-on project implementing a complete CI pipeline using Azure DevOps
- Build, test, and package stages

---

### Day 16 — Project: CD (Continuous Delivery) with Azure DevOps
- Hands-on project adding the CD stage to the Day 15 CI pipeline
- Target environment: Azure Virtual Machine
- Docker containers used for packaging; VM as deployment target

---

### Day 17 — AKS (Azure Kubernetes Service)
- What is AKS and how it differs from self-managed Kubernetes
- Deploying a two-tier application on AKS
- Exposing the application to the external world
- Ingress configuration on AKS

---

### Day 18 — Large Project: Three-Tier E-Commerce Application on AKS
Full end-to-end project:
- 8 microservices
- 2 databases
- Messaging queue
- Caching service
- Writing Dockerfiles for each service
- Service-to-service communication
- Complete deployment workflow
- Ingress configuration
- Target platform: AKS

---

### Day 19 — Interview Q&A: Azure DevOps
Dedicated interview questions and answers covering:
- Azure DevOps concepts (Days 14–18)
- CI/CD pipelines
- AKS

> Second self-evaluation checkpoint.

---

### Day 20 — Azure Key Vault
- Storing and managing sensitive information (secrets, keys, certificates) on Azure
- Azure's equivalent to AWS Secrets Manager / SSM Parameter Store

---

### Day 21 — Azure Serverless (Functions)
Serverless from a DevOps engineer's perspective — two real-world projects:
1. **Cloud Cost Optimization** — automated detection of unused/stale resources
2. **Compliance Enforcement** — automated detection of policy violations

> Both projects are resume-worthy and frequently asked about in interviews.

---

### Day 22 — Terraform with Azure
- Connecting Terraform to Azure
- Creating Azure resources using Terraform (HCL)
- Managing Terraform state file with Azure backend
- Builds on Terraform fundamentals from the DevOps series

---

### Day 23 — *(Additional Azure topic — TBD in series)*

---

### Day 24 — *(Additional Azure topic — TBD in series)*

---

### Day 25 — Interview Preparation & Course Wrap-Up
- How to present these projects on a resume
- How to explain real-world hands-on experience in interviews
- How to position yourself for Azure DevOps job roles
- Final certification readiness review

---

## Certification Alignment

### AZ-900 (Azure Fundamentals)

| Exam Domain | Weightage | Coverage in This Series |
|---|---|---|
| Cloud Concepts | 25–30% | Day 1 |
| Azure Architecture & Services | 35–40% | Days 2–18 |
| Azure Management & Governance | 30–35% | Days 13, 20, 21 |

### AZ-104 (Azure Administrator)

| Exam Domain | Coverage in This Series |
|---|---|
| Virtual Networks | Days 5–6 |
| Storage | Day 9 |
| Compute | Days 4, 17, 18 |
| Identity | Day 12 |
| Security | Days 6, 12, 20 |
| Governance | Days 21 (Compliance & Cost Optimization) |

